Compile gzip's argv[0] mode detection back in.

gzip.c picks the mode from the command name (gunzip -> decompress, zcat ->
decompress to stdout, uncompress -> decompress) only inside `#if
!GNU_STANDARD`, and GNU_STANDARD defaults to 1, so a stock build leaves that
block out and relies on the gunzip/zcat/uncompress shell scripts. We drop the
scripts and ship one `gzip` binary with gunzip/zcat/uncompress as aliases, so
the default is flipped to 0 in the source.

It is not passed as -DGNU_STANDARD=0 because gzip's nixpkgs derivation sets
its flags through `env`, which must not overlap the pipeline's own top-level
NIX_CFLAGS_COMPILE.

--- a/gzip.c
+++ b/gzip.c
@@ -429,7 +429,7 @@
     opterr = !env;
 
 #ifndef GNU_STANDARD
-# define GNU_STANDARD 1
+# define GNU_STANDARD 0
 #endif
 #if !GNU_STANDARD
     /* For compatibility with old compress, use program name as an option.
